\f1\b\fs24 \cf0 That\'92s much closer to what I think you\'92re looking for.
\f0\b0 \
The source can remain a textbook, paper, article or documentation. We don\'92t need to replace text as an information-delivery medium. Instead, we insert a transformation layer between 
\f1\b source material
\f0\b0  and 
\f1\b your mental model
\f0\b0 .\
And I think there\'92s an especially promising rule here:\

\f1\b Don\'92t visualize sentences. Extract the system described by the sentences.
\f0\b0 \
That\'92s a considerably more powerful idea than automatic mind mapping.\
